 Full-text search runs in the database, not Elasticsearch. On MySQL it is sharded 16 ways by CRC32 of the account ID (`Search::Record::Trilogy`); on SQLite it is a single FTS5 index (`Search::Record::SQLite`). Don't assume the sharded shape when working under SQLite. Models in `app/models/search/`.
 
+### Storage Usage
+
+`Account#bytes_used` and `Board#bytes_used` count card images and files embedded in board descriptions, card descriptions, and comments:
+- Attachment changes append `Storage::Entry` deltas in the same transaction, so busy accounts never contend for a counter row
+- `Storage::MaterializeJob` adds pending entries to each owner's `Storage::Total` in the background and deletes them, so reads are a single lookup
+- Reconciliation recalculates totals from scratch: after imports (which bypass callbacks), daily for recently changed accounts, and via `bin/rails storage:reconcile`
+- Models in `app/models/storage/`, `app/models/concerns/storage/`; attachment hooks in `lib/rails_ext/active_storage_attachment_storage_tracking.rb`
+
 ### Imports and exports
 
 Allow people to move between OSS and SAAS Fizzy instances:
